 "story": "Liverpool beat LASK Linz 6-3 at the Raiffeisen Arena, a win that lifted them to fifth in the Champions League table. Ronald Araujo put Liverpool ahead in the 22nd minute, and Bradley Barcola made it 2-0 two minutes later. Barcola made it 3-0 in the 37th minute, which was the half-time score. Jeremie Frimpong made it 4-0 in the 51st minute, and Robert Ljubicic, who came off the bench for Melayro Bogarde, pulled one back for LASK Linz in the 63rd. Barcola made it 5-1 in the 66th minute and Lewis Koumas made it 6-1 in the 72nd, both set up by Frimpong, before Florian Flecker, who came off the bench for Kasper Jørgensen, scored in the 74th and 77th minutes. Liverpool had 26 shots to LASK Linz's 12.",
